---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const run = "https://github.com/sachncs/axiom/actions/runs/37202924572";
---
<section class="section shell evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
  <div class="evidence__head">
    <span class="eyebrow">Current qualification · Linux resource gate</span>
    <h2 id="evidence-title">Measure the system<br /><span class="gradient-text">that ships now.</span></h2>
    <p>Historical native-engine rates are not evidence for today’s paper modes. The current 512 MiB address-space qualification exposes unresolved memory failures.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="evidence__grid">
    <article class="evidence__card">
      <span class="evidence__state">Basic · incomplete</span>
      <h3>Updates complete.<br />Recovery still fails.</h3>
      <p>1,000,000 durable updates in 110.443 seconds (~9,054/s), with 14,971 partner queries and backup completed. Disk-pressure recovery then raised <code>MemoryError</code> rebuilding System indexes.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="evidence__card evidence__card--alert">
      <span class="evidence__state">Multilevel · failed</span>
      <h3>Startup exceeds<br />the resource cap.</h3>
      <p>The million-vertex service could not finish its initial matching refresh under the 512 MiB address-space limit. This run does not qualify startup, updates, or recovery.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <div class="evidence__foot">
    <span class="mono">Run 37202924572 · 512 MiB address cap · 192 MiB ext4 volume</span>
    <a class="text-link" href={run}>Inspect workflow logs ↗</a>
  </div>
  <p class="evidence__scope">The Basic figures come from this run’s Basic matrix job; its later recovery step failed. These are constrained resource diagnostics, not a throughput qualification or production-readiness claim. The 10k durable updates/s target remains unproven for Basic and Multilevel.</p>
  <a class="evidence__more" href={`${base}/upcoming/`}>See the alpha roadmap →</a>
</section>
<style>
  .evidence { padding-block: 38px 68px; }
  .evidence__head { max-width: 760px; }
  .evidence h2 { font-size: clamp(30px,3.3vw,44px); line-height:1.1; letter-spacing:-.045em; margin:24px 0 18px; }
  .evidence__head > p { color:var(--ink-dim); font-size:16px; max-width:690px; }
  .evidence__grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:16px; margin-top:32px; }
  .evidence__card { border:1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius:var(--r-xl); padding:clamp(22px,3vw,34px); background:var(--bg-2); }
  .evidence__card--alert { border-color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--amber) 52%, var(--line)); }
  .evidence__state { font:11px var(--font-mono); color:var(--cobalt); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em; }
  .evidence__card--alert .evidence__state { color:var(--amber); }
  .evidence h3 { font-size:clamp(22px,2.6vw,31px); line-height:1.14; letter-spacing:-.035em; margin:20px 0 12px; }
  .evidence__card p { color:var(--ink-dim); font-size:14px; line-height:1.7; margin:0; }
  .evidence__foot { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; gap:12px; padding-top:20px; margin-top:20px; border-top:1px solid var(--line); }
  .evidence__foot .mono { color:var(--ink-faint); font-size:10px; }
  .evidence__scope { max-width:780px; color:var(--ink-faint); font-size:12px; line-height:1.7; margin:18px 0 10px; }
  .evidence__more { color:var(--cobalt); font-size:13px; font-weight:650; }
  @media(max-width:700px) { .evidence__grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
</style>
